      "review_notes": "The independent target is a Poisson mixture of finite sums of independent signed jumps. A finite product-map law supplies the accumulator expectation; the main expectation conditions on the independent Poisson count. The CTE loop is natural induction and one abstract callback call per jump. Tests explicitly use negative deterministic jumps, a negative accumulated total, zero Poisson rate, infinite credits and resource framing. A generic caller specializes the latent type to integers with jump=id, ensuring the theorem covers arbitrary signed jump laws."
    },
