      "review_notes": "The canonical signed difference of two independent Poisson counts is a measurable image of their product law. The central expectation is the standard map/product integral, and the program logic consists of the two verified Poisson calls and subtraction. Independent tests check both rates zero, a zero left rate producing a nonpositive integer law, infinite credit and resource framing."
